        <technology>
            <technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses xml:lang="en">The glass sheet is heated to a temperature just below its softening point (about 640°C) and then immediately cooled by special jets of cold-air. These harden the surface of the glass, giving the inside more time to cool. This allows the external layer to crystallize into a wider lattice while the inside solidifies with greater compression than in the crystal lattice.\n\n# Included processes\nGate to gate inventory for the process not including infrastructure and emissions.</technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>
        </technology>
    </processInformation>
